                     /GO_process="GO:0015697 - quaternary ammonium group
                     transport [Evidence IEA]"
                     /note="Members of the family are the ATP-binding subunit
                     of ABC transporters for substrates such as betaine,
                     L-proline or other amino acids, choline, carnitine, etc.
                     The substrate specificity is best determined from the
                     substrate-binding subunit, rather than this subunit, as it
                     interacts with the permease subunit and not with substrate
                     directly.; Members of the family are the ATP-binding
                     subunit of ABC transporters for substrates such as
                     betaine, L-proline or other amino acids, choline,
                     carnitine, etc. The substrate specificity is best
                     determined from the substrate-binding subunit, rather than
                     this subunit, as it interacts with the permease subunit
                     and not with substrate directly.; Members of the family
                     are the ATP-binding subunit of ABC transporters for
                     substrates such as betaine, L-proline or other amino
                     acids, choline, carnitine, etc. The substrate specificity
                     is best determined from the substrate-binding subunit,
